  "control_reading": "Control-level observation, NOT a task property: with a learning-rate sweep (2 LRs) and 3 seeds, the dense H=64 control's terminal KL at 3200 updates is 0.0655-0.0889 in all 12 cells -- above eps_abs = 0.05 -- with 1600->3200 gaps of 0.0005-0.0118. This shows the control does not saturate within 2x budget at two learning rates. It does NOT establish that the task family has genuine terminal headroom: two LRs and one budget doubling cannot exclude a shared optimiser floor, and the analytic shape cost (0.063 nat) already exceeds eps_abs and sits only 0.0025 below the smallest observed terminal KL.",
