    "reading": "No advantage was detected for the block mask under this manipulation: D<0 in all six condition-by-seed pairs, interaction point estimate +0.0059 with sd 0.0211 and a 95% t-interval [-0.0466, +0.0584]. This is NOT a demonstration that organisation is harmful: density matching fixes only the nonzero count, so mask placement is confounded with cross-group mixing, and D<0 also holds in F where the block mask matches the task's group structure -- the pattern a generic mixing or optimisation effect predicts. With three seeds the interval still contains delta_min = 0.05, so the honest label is 'no signal at the frozen minimum useful effect', not 'the effect is absent'."
